{
  "id": "62f89770-2a44-4dde-b654-a8477fbff0cb",
  "page_title": "'Quickstart: Use the OpenAI Service image generation Go SDK'",
  "page_description": "Walkthrough on how to get started with Azure OpenAI image generation using the Go SDK.",
  "page_date": "08/28/2023",
  "chunk_title": "Generate images with DALL-E",
  "chunk_content": "Generate images with DALL-E  Open *sample.go* in your preferred code editor.  Add the following code to your script:  ```go package main  import ( \t\"context\" \t\"fmt\" \t\"net/http\" \t\"os\"  \t\"github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/ai/azopenai\" \t\"github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/azcore/to\" )  func main() { \tazureOpenAIKey := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY\")  \t// Ex: \"https://<your-azure-openai-host>.openai.azure.com\" \tazureOpenAIEndpoint := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT\")  \tif azureOpenAIKey == \"\" || azureOpenAIEndpoint == \"\" { \t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Skipping example, environment variables missing\\n\") \t\treturn \t}  \tkeyCredential, err := azopenai.NewKeyCredential(azureOpenAIKey)  \tif err != nil { \t\t// handle error \t}  \tclient, err := azopenai.NewClientWithKeyCredential(azureOpenAIEndpoint, keyCredential, nil)  \tif err != nil { \t\t// handle error \t}  \tresp, err := client.CreateImage(context.TODO(), azopenai.ImageGenerationOptions{ \t\tPrompt:         to.Ptr(\"a painting of a cat in the style of Dali\"), \t\tResponseFormat: to.Ptr(azopenai.ImageGenerationResponseFormatURL), \t}, nil)  \tif err != nil { \t\t// handle error \t}  \tfor _, generatedImage := range resp.Data { \t\t// the underlying type for the generatedImage is dictated by the value of \t\t// ImageGenerationOptions.ResponseFormat. In this example we used `azopenai.ImageGenerationResponseFormatURL`, \t\t// so the underlying type will be ImageLocation.  \t\tresp, err := http.Head(*generatedImage.URL)  \t\tif err != nil { \t\t\t// handle error \t\t}  \t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Image generated, HEAD request on URL returned %d\\nImage URL: %s\\n\", resp.StatusCode, *generatedImage.URL) \t} } ```  Run the script using the `go run` command:  ```console go run sample.go ```",
